  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [activation notification](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation-notification) spec says as following.\n>When a user interaction causes firing of an [activation triggering input event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation-triggering-input-event) in a [Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#document) document, the user agent must perform the following activation notification steps before [dispatching](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch) the event:\n\nBut it is not quite clear what does it means by in a `Document` document. I suppose a quite plausible definition would refer the document to be the node document of the event target. ",
